  "question": {
    "text": "<p>An ideal gas in a thermally insulated vessel at internal pressure = <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> , volume = <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and absolute temperature = <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> expands irreversibly against zero external pressure, as shown in the diagram. The final internal pressure, volume and absolute temperature of the gas are <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> , <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> , respectively. For this expansion,<br ><br/><img src=\"assets\\qt0023_4612139d4cbd.jpg\"/></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math>",
